The Derwent Remediation Project is the world’s largest holistic river remediation project. 
The estuary remediation contains a minimum of 8.5 million cubic metres of contaminated sediment and the catchment covers 15,486 square kilometres.

Our aim is to use the Derwent Remediation Project as a showcase for the world to:
  - develop the technical, business & investment models for holistic river remediation;
  - mobilise institutional capital for large river remediation and;
  - develop a multi-trillion dollar global river remediation industry.
